00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:10.230
The infamous K-1 Visa is in the spotlight,

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.000
thanks to the mega popular
show, the "90 Day Fiance"

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.480
and it's apparently never-ending
number of spin-offs,

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.867
like the "90 Day Fiance: The Other Way"

00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:20.737
"Happily Ever After", "Before the 90 Days"

00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:24.327
"90 Days of Facebook Chats",
"Say Yes! To the 90 Days"

00:00:24.327 --> 00:00:26.600
"We Found Love Thanks
To Google Translate",

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.080
and the "4 Hour Work Fiance".

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.160
Leave it to TLC to turn a
complicated immigration process

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.310
into a hit reality show.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.820
The premise of the "90 Day Fiance"

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.940
is that an American citizen falls in love

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.980
with someone from another country.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.640
Once the couple is engaged,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.600
the U.S. immigration law allows the fiance

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.340
to enter the country legally.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:48.350
The process for this is known
as the non-immigrant visa,

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:52.110
also referred to by its
formal name, the K-1 Visa.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:53.980
Obviously, Americans can't get enough

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.180
of international relationships.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.013
In this video though,

00:00:57.013 --> 00:00:58.610
we're going to be talking about love,

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.570
marriage, and international travel,

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:04.874
and the legality of the
"90-Day Fiance's" K-1 Visa.

00:01:04.874 --> 00:01:08.330
(trumpet sounds)

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.720
Hey Legal Eagles, it's
time to think like a lawyer

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.100
because even crappy reality T.V shows

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.170
implicate complex legal issues.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.010
The fiance non-immigrant visa,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.770
is the document an American citizen needs

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:22.350
to bring his or her foreign
fiance to the United States.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.330
The K-1 Visa permits the
foreign citizen fiance

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.670
to travel to United States

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.370
and marry his or her U.S. citizen sponsor

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.470
within 90 days of arrival.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.870
Once married, the foreign
citizen will then apply

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:37.260
for adjustment of status to
lawful permanent resident

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.690
and can stay in the United
States as long as they like.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.370
Who can get the K-1 Visa?

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.700
Well, the first requirement
is that the U.S. citizen

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.130
and fiance must be
legally allowed to marry

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.530
at the time of the petition
for the K-1 Visa was filed.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:50.860
Marriage laws differ of course,

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.070
from country to country
and state to state.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.610
So to get a K-1 Visa,

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.420
the marriage has to be legally possible

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.720
according to the laws of the United States

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.330
and the state in which the
marriage will take place.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.050
Now the second requirement
is that the couple

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.447
must have actually met in person.

00:02:05.447 --> 00:02:07.580
"90-Day Finance" fans often ask

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:08.950
whether the government cares at all

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.060
about how much time these
people spend with each other

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.370
before applying for K-1 and
coming to the United States.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.810
The answer is that generally,

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:19.060
the foreign citizen fiance
and the U.S. citizen sponsor

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.010
must have actually met in person

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.190
at least once within the past two years.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.730
It's probably not too much to
ask when you think about it.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.090
Although the U.S. government
can grant an exception

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.630
to this requirement for extreme hardship,

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.760
it is extremely rare for this
requirement to be waived.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.740
We have seen lots of examples of people

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.710
not knowing each other for very long

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:42.310
before applying for the
fiance visa on the show.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:45.640
Robert from the most season
of the, "90-Day Fiance"

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.760
probably takes the cake.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.070
He met his Dominican
fiance Anny on Facebook

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:53.190
and then scheduled a cruise
to meet her in person.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.940
- And she's hot.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.330
- Robert then left the cruise for a trip

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.640
and spent a whopping eight hours with her

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.390
before deciding that
this Cardi-B look alike

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:04.000
was his dream woman.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.630
- For people who think this is crazy,

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:08.110
I say, "what the hell,
mind your business."

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.460
- I guess it was love at first ship.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.160
Their meeting took slightly less time

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:15.530
than it takes to register a
new car at DMV, but guess what?

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.010
Robert and Anny's quick trip

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.830
met the bare minimum
requirement for the K-1 Visa.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.150
And there have been several couples

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.540
who use mobile phone apps to
communicate with each other

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.873
because neither speaks the
other person's language.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:29.020
- (speaking in foreign language)

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.230
- [Interpreter] I want
to talk about our future.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.630
- But I think we can all agree that "Love"

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.120
is the universal language.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.740
So how does one apply for a K-1 Visa?

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.600
Well, the application process is long

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:40.840
and it can be very arduous.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.160
You need a lot of paperwork
to get the ball rolling,

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.800
including an online
non-immigrant visa application,

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.490
plus additional forms if
the person has children,

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:51.270
a passport, a birth certificate,

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.100
divorce certificates if applicable,

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.540
police certificates from
everywhere the fiance has lived

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.110
since the age of 16,

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.850
medical examination, photographs,

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:02.310
evidence of the relationship,
and payment of fees.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.860
And that there's just one more thing,

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.990
evidence of financial support.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:09.030
This is actually pretty big deal.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.000
U.S. politicians frequently make claims

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.397
about the immigration process

00:04:12.397 --> 00:04:14.070
and that they worry
that the people who come

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:17.700
to United States, will be a
financial burden on the country.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.490
But to some extent
immigration laws already have

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.830
strict requirements about
financial responsibility

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.570
when you come to United States.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.020
During their visa interview

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:29.400
applicants must produce evidence
to the councilor office,

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.720
that they will not become a public charge

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:32.740
in the United States.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:35.560
Public charge refers to
being unable to provide

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.600
basic necessities of living like housing,

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.480
food, shelter, and clothing.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.530
If a person will become a public charge

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.030
the visa will be denied

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.010
and that person cannot enter the country.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.380
Now the evidence of financial
support could be information

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.850
showing the person can't
financially support themselves

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:52.560
for instance, if the
person has a job lined up

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.760
or has a lucrative career as a model,

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.910
or they just happened
to be incredibly rich.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.150
Since this is likely not
the case for most people,

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.990
they must be able to show
that the U.S. citizen

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.530
can provide financial support.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.680
The American citizen will
have to file an affidavit

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.930
stating that he or she

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:08.820
will be able to support their new spouse

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:12.060
and any children who come
over with that new fiance.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.580
This is a legally binding contract.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.200
If the person, the citizen is sponsoring

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.280
becomes a public charge

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.560
and the government has to public services,

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.040
the agency providing the help

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.800
can sue the American
citizen to recover the cost.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.710
So how does the U.S government decide

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:27.700
whether someone will
become a public charge?

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.640
There are many factors, a person's age,

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.990
education, work
experience, skills, assets,

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.070
financial resources and health,

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.890
they're are all taken into account.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.130
And we've seen how the allegation

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:39.550
of a public charge possibility

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.960
has impacted the somewhat happy couples.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.730
When Nicole, a single mother,

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.270
who struggles to make ends meet

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:48.560
fell in love with man from Morocco,

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:50.380
she knew she would be unable to meet

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.560
the financial requirements
for the K-1 Visa,

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.210
but her father decided to co-sponsor Azan

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:57.503
and the government gave him a visa.

00:05:57.503 --> 00:05:59.220
- I think he sounded sincere,

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.353
he sounded like he
wants to be with Nicole.

00:06:01.353 --> 00:06:02.943
- He's a good guy and
you guys will see that

00:06:02.943 --> 00:06:04.410
when you get to meet him.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:08.050
- Paul has appeared on two
seasons of "90-day Fiance."

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:10.250
Paul is a Kentucky man in his late 30s

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.720
who fell in love with
Brazilian woman name Karine.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.030
- Are you excited to meet me,

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:15.520
you excited that I'm coming to Brazil?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.650
- I don't understand.

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.810
- Oh no, she's doesn't understand,

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:20.643
that's not good.

00:06:20.643 --> 00:06:22.010
- Despite their age difference,

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:24.260
12 years and language problems,

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:27.610
neither speak the other person's language,

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:29.230
they fell in love.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.840
Paul and Karine first appeared
on "Before the 90 days"

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:33.760
which chronical Paul's
efforts to bring Karine

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.760
to the United States.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.330
Paul inquired about
bringing Karine to America

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.610
on a K-1 Visa, but he ran into trouble

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:42.330
because he's a grown ass
man living with his parents

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.050
who doesn't really work.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.380
- I'm definitely a mama's boy,

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.150
I will say that.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:47.983
I love you.

00:06:47.983 --> 00:06:50.780
- I know, love you too Paul.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:53.060
- Financial affidavit
requires proof of income,

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:55.640
three years of tax
returns, bank statements,

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.400
employee verification,

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.760
and lots of other stuff
that Paul didn't have.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.080
And Paul's mom wasn't
about to sign the papers

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.880
necessary to support Karine.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:06.320
- I think it's all crazy myself, really.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.760
- When Karine got pregnant,

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.990
the couple then appeared
on "90-Day the other way"

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.850
where Paul decided to go live

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:15.830
in Karine's very remote
Brazilian home town.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.880
The hapless Pauls exploits in Brazil

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.750
included worrying about
whether deadly fish

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.530
will be able to swim up his urethra,

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:24.210
and carrying a mosquito
net with him everywhere.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.550
- Better to have it and not need it

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:26.670
than need it then not have it.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.330
- The relationship might not have worked

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:30.810
but it made for some fantastic television.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:31.957
- Chickens (Paul clucking).

00:07:33.374 --> 00:07:34.930
- (laughs)

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.840
- Now one of the highlights
of his story line

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:38.410
was Paul running into the jungle

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:39.440
after the government of Brazil

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.290
denied him the right to live permanently

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.070
in the country of Brazil.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:46.390
The reason, Paul has a
felony conviction for arson.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:48.700
- The second case, my ex-girlfriend and I

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:51.530
both took out restraining
orders against each other.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.050
- Just a quality human being,

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:55.100
and as you can see other
countries also have

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.660
immigration standards.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.330
But love conquers all.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.190
So that left the couple
back where they started,

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:02.290
trying to assure the U.S. government

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.610
that Paul can financially
support his family

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.090
if they come to United States.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:08.580
Now that Paul's mom has grandchildren,

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:11.260
she maybe more willing to
sign that financial affidavit.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.690
I'm told you should definitely stay tuned.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.740
Now "90-Day" fans are always
on the look out for people

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.930
abusing the finance application process.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:21.860
Is this true love or just a foreigner

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:23.240
looking for a green card?

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:25.700
Is the American citizen
sketchy in dangling the visa

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:28.310
as leverage to control
their foreign finance?

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:30.550
Well, Congress has long been concerned

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:33.870
about the possibility of abuse
and fraud, and exploitation

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:36.620
from both the U.S. citizen
and the foreign fiance.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:40.040
In 2005, Congress enacted
the International Marriage

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.240
Broker Regulation Act

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:44.460
to reduce the abuse of
marriage based visa recipients.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.930
The law adds a few safeguards
to the screening process

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:49.060
that are intended to protect
both the visa applicant

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:50.420
and the U.S. petitioner.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.250
For example, if the American petitioner

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:54.190
used a foreign marriage broker,

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:56.267
which are the companies that
are often referred to as,

00:08:56.267 --> 00:08:58.390
"Mail-Order Bride" Companies,

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.260
they have to disclose it
to the U.S. government

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:03.150
and the broker must meet
certain strict requirements,

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:06.120
not as strict as building
new housing in San Francisco

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:07.760
but still kind of onerous.

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:10.350
All U.S. petitioners must
undergo a background check

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:13.400
and the results must be shared
with the immigrant fiance.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.000
This helps protect a foreign fiance

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.460
from arriving in the United States

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:19.496
to discover that the American
fiance is a criminal.

00:09:19.496 --> 00:09:21.712
- And I say, "I can't
come you crazy old man

00:09:21.712 --> 00:09:23.147
"I don't have green card,"

00:09:23.147 --> 00:09:26.227
and he say, "Screw green
cards, they're for poor people

00:09:26.227 --> 00:09:27.530
"just get over here."

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:29.570
- U.S. law also mandates
that if a petitioner

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:32.390
has committed specific
violent or sex crimes,

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:34.860
they cannot petition for K-1 Visa.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:37.850
These are crimes like
homicide, stalking, assault,

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:40.610
domestic violence, kidnapping
and human trafficking.

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:43.390
And what about if the foreign
fiance has a criminal record?

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.340
Well, if the fiance has a criminal record,

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:48.730
in most cases, the person will
be ineligible for the visa

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.120
or to enter the United States at all.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:53.400
This is even true when the person's crimes

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.530
have been expunged.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:57.650
Even misdemeanor convictions
can make a person in eligible,

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:59.730
these crimes are listed in Section 212

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:01.480
of the Immigration &amp; Nationality Act.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.630
They include crimes of moral turpitude,

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:06.470
a violation of any drug
law, U.S or foreign,

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:07.980
any kind of drug trafficking,

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.770
even if it doesn't result in a conviction,

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:13.370
prostitution or participating
in prostitution in any way,

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.130
participating in human trafficking,

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:18.230
whether directly or indirectly
and money laundering.

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:20.010
Now, there are some
exceptions to the rules,

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.470
a person may apply for a
waiver of a drug offense

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:23.650
if it was a single offense

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:25.300
of simple possession of marijuana,

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:28.110
and if the conviction
was over 15 years old

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:29.960
before applying for the visa.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:31.530
But the U.S. has to be satisfied

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:33.380
that the person was rehabilitated,

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.610
the person seeking the
waiver also has to show

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.030
that admission to the U.S.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.230
would not be contrary
to the national welfare,

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:41.500
safety or security of the United States.

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:44.340
If your overseas fiance was
convicted of only one crime

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:46.510
and the maximum penalty
possible for that crime

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:47.770
is less than one year,

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:50.830
he or she might not need the
waiver of inadmissibility.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.640
This exception does not take into account

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.700
the actual sentence
length given to the person

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:56.390
but rather the maximum penalty

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:58.880
that could have been given
as a result of the crime.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.730
The sentencing exception does not apply

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.250
however to drug crimes.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:04.900
Now the "90 day fiance" has
several different couples

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:07.150
impacted by one person's criminal history.

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:09.870
Let's take a look at the
situation for Tiffany and Ronald

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.520
from "90 day the other way".

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.490
Tiffany is an American
who went to South Africa

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:16.200
and fell in love with Ronald,

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.910
Ronald turned out to have a pretty serious

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.220
history of gambling.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.630
- I was at my rock bottom,

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:24.300
I had a full blown addiction of gambling.

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:26.160
- He has been charged with armed robbery,

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:29.070
theft and possession of
drugs during a traffic stop.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:31.310
And Ronald's addiction was so bad

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:33.060
that he wound up selling off his mother's

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:35.070
kitchen appliances, got arrested

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:38.160
and the adjudication was delayed
so he could attend rehab.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:40.080
Tiffany, who wasn't even fully aware

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.430
of the full extent of Ronald's issues,

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.240
moved with her son Daniel to South Africa.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.580
Once she learned the truth,

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.360
she decided to marry Ronald anyway,

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:50.310
and the two tied the knot just days

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.140
after he moved out of rehab.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:53.180
When Tiffany got pregnant,

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.390
she decided she couldn't
stand living in South Africa,

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:57.060
so she returned to the U.S.

00:11:57.060 --> 00:11:58.610
Now where does this leave Ronald

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.120
her drug and gambling addicted husband?

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.070
- His record's a little funky.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.430
There's quite a bit on there.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:06.060
- Well, at the most recent tele,

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:07.960
Tiffany announced that she
is starting the process

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:11.070
to bring Ronald to the
U.S. on a spousal visa.

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:13.760
When she discussed this with a
lawyer on an earlier episode,

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:15.820
the lawyer explained that
Ronald's arrest history

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:19.060
would be problematic for him
to come to the United States,

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:21.300
even without an actual conviction.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.930
- If there's anywhere in his
record that he admitted it,

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.510
that is an admission

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:29.960
for which he can be
determined inadmissible.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.600
- Tiffany however, feels confident

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.530
that this history won't matter.

00:12:33.530 --> 00:12:35.050
Because she erroneously believes

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.240
that "Love" is stronger than lawyers.

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:39.590
But in this particular instance
Tiffany might be right,

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:40.960
violations of gambling laws

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:43.420
are not generally considered
crimes of moral turpitude,

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:45.890
Ronald's other charges could
present problems however,

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:47.430
especially the drug charge,

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:50.670
the USCIS will have to
review the full extent

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:52.600
of his South African arrest,

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:55.200
before they decide if he
can come to United States.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:58.780
Now, the show also includes
couples who are already married,

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:00.370
people who married a foreign spouse

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.190
can apply for a CR-1 VISA

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:04.790
to allow them to immigrate to America.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:06.250
People who apply for the CR-1

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:09.560
must satisfy most of the same
requirements as the K-1 Visa

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:11.360
including a clean criminal record,

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:13.890
and proving that they
have financial support.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:15.650
Now traditionally, it was easy to bring

00:13:15.650 --> 00:13:18.080
a foreign born spouse to America.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:19.890
However, that has changed in recent years

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:22.730
largely due to the Trump
administration's travel ban.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:25.250
The travel ban restricts
immigration from countries

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.960
deemed dangerous including Iran, Libya,

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:29.810
Somalia, Syria, Yemen,

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:32.160
North Korea and Venezuela.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.550
We've already seen how
this plays out in the show,

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:37.990
a 19 year old Avery was a
self described party girl

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:42.210
from Columbus, Ohio, until
she met Omar a Syrian online.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.920
The two fell in love and
she converted to Islam,

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.910
and Avery married Omar
on a trip to Lebanon.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:52.000
This means she didn't need to
apply for a K-1 Fiance Visa.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.850
And although Avery's mother
kind of sorta supports

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:56.030
the relationship,

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.160
- Oh my gosh.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:59.560
- She's highly uncomfortable
with the idea of her daughter

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.660
moving to Syria to live with Omar,

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:04.120
even though he insists
that this part of Syria

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:05.400
is pretty safe.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:08.360
- The whole country is in the
middle of civil war Avery.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.270
- I personally think
you're worrying too much.

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:12.400
- Eventually the couple
decided that the best thing

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:14.270
would be for Omar to come to the U.S.

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:16.730
So they applied for the CR-1 Visa,

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:18.920
which is for an immigrant spouse.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.140
Unfortunately for the
couple, the travel ban

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:24.010
restricts the number of
Syrians who can enter the U.S.

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:26.670
even if they are married
to an American citizen.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:28.890
- The lawyer has worked on,

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:30.940
he said many travel ban cases

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:34.080
and none of them have been approved.

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:37.280
- A CR-1 Visa is supposed
to be easy to obtain

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:39.170
but the Supreme Court
okayed the travel ban

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:40.960
in part because the Trump administration

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:42.410
said it would grant waivers

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:44.460
if a couple experienced undue hardship,

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:47.120
and the foreign spouse was
basically not a terrorist.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.810
In practice, though the waiver
has been harder to obtain,

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.300
the Trump administration has been vague

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:53.610
about what constitutes an undue hardship.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:55.110
According to the Trump administration,

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:58.340
fewer than 5% of people
who apply for waivers

00:14:58.340 --> 00:14:59.670
have been approved,

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.760
and of this 5% who were approved

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:04.200
the government is in no
rush to provide the visas,

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:07.190
over one third of those
who have been approved

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:08.850
are still awaiting the visa.

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:10.840
That's why some are finding their spouse

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:14.270
an administrative Limbo,
instead of being denied,

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:17.150
the case is placed in
administrative processing

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:18.950
where it may sit for many years.

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:21.300
And although Avery and Omar have indicated

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:23.590
that Omar's application was accepted,

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:25.740
that just means the government
is reviewing the petition

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.250
to enter the country.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.100
As a lawyer explained to Avery,

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:30.930
Omar is going to need that waiver

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:33.330
if he has any hope of getting
into the United states.

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:36.540
Now admittedly, lots of "90
day" fans are claiming that TLC

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.890
told that lawyer to lie about Omar's hopes

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:40.630
of getting into United States,

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:42.500
but the lawyer's probably right here.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.300
As the form shows Omar's petition

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:46.260
has been accepted for processing,

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:48.030
but it says right on
the bottom of the form

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:49.330
that it is not a visa,

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:52.280
it will still be an uphill
battle for him to be admitted.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:55.090
Now there are limitations on the K-1 Visa.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.410
A person who enters the U.S.

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:59.170
has 90 days to marry a U.S. citizen

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:01.980
but only that particular U.S. citizen.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:04.910
If a guy like Syngin from
the new season of "90 days"

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:07.730
decides that Tania is
not really his cup of tea

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:10.140
and he'd rather marry another American,

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:12.010
he will have to leave the country

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:14.160
and start the whole
process all over again.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.310
And it looks like American citizen Rebecca

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:17.640
from "Before the 90 days

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.080
is on her second K-1 Visa.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.040
Rebecca was in the middle of a divorce

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:23.630
from her Moroccan born husband

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:27.760
when she met Zeid, a 26
year old from Tunisia.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:32.760
- Oh my god, I love you
so much, I love you more.

00:16:33.048 --> 00:16:34.020
- He's amazing.

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:35.770
- Rebecca who is a private investigator

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:38.190
has now applied for the K-1 Visa for Zeid,

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:39.950
and she better make this one count

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:42.860
since a U.S. citizen is
limited to two K-1 Visas

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:44.710
during their entire lifetime.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:48.600
This limitation protects foreign
fiance's from exploitation,

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:51.420
because if a U.S. citizen
could apply for K-1 Visas

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:52.730
whenever they felt like it,

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:54.410
they could lure people into the country

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:55.910
with false promises of marriage

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.120
and then subject that person

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.020
to involuntary servitude or worse.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:02.100
And although Rebecca's Moroccan ex

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:03.660
hasn't appeared on the show,

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.690
his legal status could be up in the air

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:07.280
because of their divorce.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:09.990
The Immigration Fraud Amendments of 1986

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:12.920
make the foreign spouses
permanent residency conditional

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.280
for two years.

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:16.640
This means that the
couples must remain married

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:19.530
for two years for the visa to stick.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.340
If a couple splits up, then the government

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:24.630
may revoke the immigrant spouses
permanent residency status.

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:26.670
This means that the
person is in the country

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.300
unlawfully and has to leave.

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:30.650
Of course, there are lots
of procedural hurdles

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:33.020
that can trip up a visa application.

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:34.850
On the brand new season of "90 day fiance"

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:36.840
we met Michael and Juliana,

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:41.840
Michael is a 42 year
"wine entrepreneur" hmm...

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.230
And Juliana is a 23 year
old Brazilian model.

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:47.620
When they met at a yacht party in Croatia

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.080
when Juliana was about 19 years old,

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:53.080
it was love at first sight, again.

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:56.250
- I don't necessarily believe
in love at first sight,

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:58.610
but it's like we were kindred spirits.

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:00.870
- Although Michael flew
around the world with Juliana,

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:04.030
she was repeatedly denied
a U.S. visitor visa.

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:06.280
The reason, her age and history

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:08.300
were red flags for prostitution.

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:11.330
The U.S. government can
deny entry to any person

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:13.880
who it suspects, is coming
to the United States

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:15.700
solely, principally or incidentally

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:17.430
to engage in prostitution,

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:20.420
or has engaged in
prostitution within 10 years

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:22.310
the date of the application for a visa,

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.650
admission or adjustment of status.

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:26.950
Juliana and Michael vehemently denied

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:30.000
that Juliana was ever an
escort or a yatch girl.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.480
Michael stresses that Juliana
was just a beautiful girl

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:34.140
from a very poor village in Brazil

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:37.300
who found love, in a
not so hopeless place,

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.300
a yacht full of rich people.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.420
- Certainly a lot of people
that may pass judgment,

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:43.680
may think I'm just an old sleazy rich guy

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:45.690
going after a young hot woman.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:47.380
It doesn't bother me at all.

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.690
- But not surprisingly,
these are the very things

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:52.070
that the government considers red flags.

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:54.190
You don't need to be
convicted of prostitution

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:55.460
to be denied entry.

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:57.790
In practice, the government
is looking carefully

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.940
at people who are working in the tourism

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:01.260
or entertainment industries.

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:04.300
Sometimes there's a very fine
line between being a model

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:06.510
and being a model who is also paid

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:08.290
to entertain clients on a boat.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.123
For example,

00:19:09.123 --> 00:19:10.603
- Um, let's talk about you,

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:13.470
what do you do for a living?

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:16.049
- Model
- a model, what kind of model

00:19:16.049 --> 00:19:17.660
- A fashion model.

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:19.490
- The government is
also actively screening

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:21.410
for victims of human trafficking.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.220
Although Juliana and Michael

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.710
protest the questions over their motives,

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:27.930
teen girls from Brazil and Thailand

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:30.180
are often lured into dangerous situations

00:19:30.180 --> 00:19:32.780
by men promising lucrative
modeling opportunities.

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:35.680
And unfortunately, escort jobs
can sometimes be the gateway

00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:36.690
or the price of admission

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:39.070
to working in entertainment and tourism.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:41.210
Of course, Michael claims
that he has already invested

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:45.150
more than $150,000 in his
relationship with Juliana,

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:47.260
there didn't seem to be much due process

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:49.050
Michael wind in the second episode,

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:50.920
which focused on Juliana's interview

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:52.980
with the U.S. immigration authorities.

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:54.550
Michael and Juliana have a lawyer

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:56.360
so I'm willing to bet
that they were well aware

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:58.640
that this question would
continue to pop up.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:19:59.880
But don't take my word for it,

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.670
just Look at this form
the I-485 application

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:03.770
for the K-1 Visa.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:07.200
As you can see question 35, 36, 37 and 38,

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:10.070
all concerned allegations of prostitution.

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:11.510
And despite the probing questions

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:13.650
eventually the government
decided that Juliana

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:16.550
had not in fact been involved
in illicit activities.

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:18.690
Now many "90 day" fans have questions

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.430
about another potential
legal hurdle to the K-1 Visa,

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:24.230
immigrants from countries
where polygamy is legal.

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:26.110
So let's see how this plays out

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:29.570
thanks to the ever popular
couple Michael and Angela.

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:32.310
Angela was a divorced grandmother of six

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:34.240
when she met Michael a Trump loving

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:37.001
30-year-old Nigerian man online.

00:20:37.001 --> 00:20:39.562
(paper rustles)

00:20:39.562 --> 00:20:40.530
- Oh, sorry.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:42.540
Angela's first visit to Nigeria

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:44.940
was featured on before the "90 days"

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:46.530
she was going to propose to Michael

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:49.490
but then she discovered
that he committed some,

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:53.150
let's say unusual sexual
indiscretions at a nightclub,

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:55.170
but the relationship was off,

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:58.390
or was it, the two spent the
rest of the season fighting,

00:20:58.390 --> 00:21:01.650
Angela accused Michael of
taking from her bank account

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:04.380
without authorization and
broke off the engagement,

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:06.650
later Angela figured out
it was a banking error

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:08.120
and Michael was back in.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:10.260
But on the next season Angela and Michael

